# Dev-only tooling — the workbench. NEVER installed on the Raspberry Pi runtime:
# the product ships from requirements.txt alone. This is the file humans edit;
# `requirements-dev.txt` beside it is generated and hashed (see README.md ->
# Dependency locking). Install locally with:
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt

# The runtime set is pulled in so both locks are resolved together: a shared
# transitive dependency (anyio, certifi, typing-extensions) then cannot land on
# one version in requirements.txt and a different one here, which is what makes
# installing dev tooling silently change the product.
-r requirements.in

